  "body": "Found in the second safety read of PR #3057 (comment 7075035960). This is behaviour from #1862 on `main`, not a defect of PR #3057.\n\n`MoveSketch` (`crates/app/src/commands/move_sketch.rs:37-42`) accepts any offset up to `MAX_OFFSET` (1e6 mm). A DXF profile that lies partly or fully off the top face of the stock is neither refused nor reported. Only the viewport shows it. The MCP tool `move_dxf_profile` behaves the same.\n\nExpected: when the placed profile leaves the top face of the stock, the Stock page, the import summary and the MCP reply show a warning that names the profile and the distance off the stock. The placement stays possible (a fixture or a later stock change can make it valid), so a warning is enough; generation keeps its own checks.\n\nTwo smaller notes from the same read:\n- The DXF units prompt does not remember which setup was active at the drop. The drawing goes to the setup that is active when the user answers.\n- No test edits \"Profile X\" in an inch document.\n",
